# H2d (SOFT, quad, THE DECISIVE RUN): the four-card sub-device probe on SEPARATE FABRIC LINKS. The first card runs (2026-10-10) showed that with a sub-device manager loaded the mesh opens, eager and
# traced gathers on each sub-device are exact, solo and chained, and that two gather streams on ONE fabric link deadlock the ring (a router has one local-worker sender channel per link and two
# clients overwrite each other's connection). This run puts the target's gathers on link 0 and the drafter's on link 1: the fabric step mounts ~/opgraft-K64j-LO/_ttnncpp.so (L1) over the image's two copies
# (read-only), exports its sha256, and the probe REFUSES to measure unless every copy it can load hashes to it and carries QWEN_AG_LINK_OFFSET_SD1 (a graft mounted is not a graft executed).
# Arms, in this order, each exact (outputs overwritten with NaN before every replay, compared against the host on every chip), each timed in a block (20 rounds after 4 warm-ups): t_solo (the target's trace of
# 24 gathers on ONE link), d_solo, t_solo2 (the same trace on TWO links: the link cost), chained (by an event), one_queue (the control), separate (BOTH concurrently: target link 0 on queue 0, drafter link 1
# on queue 1). Nothing here puts two streams on one link.
# THE RULE, registered before the run (subdev_plan.port_rule; the line carries port=...):
#   GO           'verdict=PASS-SEPARATE-LINKS' (separate concurrent wall <= 1.10 x the longer solo, every byte identical, no hang) AND link_cost = t_solo / t_solo2 <= 1.25.
#   CONDITIONAL  the same with 1.25 < link_cost <= 1.75: decide with the collective share c of the verify block (c * (link_cost - 1) <= 0.042 at the worst grid loss to 0.113 at the best; at c = 0.15 that is
#                link_cost <= 1.28 to 1.75).
#   NO-GO        anything else: a hang, a byte difference, no overlap on separate links (FAIL-SERIALISED / FAIL-PARTIAL), link_cost > 1.75; then the port goes the drafter-without-CCL way.
# READ: 'SUBDEV_H2 verdict=... separate_ratio=... link_cost=... port=...' and the JSON (kind subdev-h2: report['port_rule'], report['graft'], every arm's walls, every byte comparison).
# TIMED: pause the ARC runners. A hang wedges the mesh: Z resets. Duration (estimate): 35 min (the box bounds the probe; the fabric step's own limit is 45).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the separate-links run of the sub-device overlap programme (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the window branch (a branch that carries optimisation/ttnn-op/subdev_h and scripts/ci/tp4_subdev_probe.py) and push a tag
# experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed
# from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the read rules and the minutes. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag of the window's own
# image (sed -i 's/tp4-next2-1/<tag>/' *.env). The cards are under development: nothing here stops, starts or hands back the node agent.

C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset fabric
C2_FABRIC_PROBE=subdev-links
C2_FABRIC=FABRIC_1D
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=40
